+## Phase 4 owned ordered indexes
+
+The independent mab_structures library uses signed-int32 keys and size_t payloads.
+SkipList and BTree implement OrderedIndex: insert returns whether a unique key was
+added, duplicate insertion preserves the first payload, find returns a copied
+payload/absence, and size counts unique keys. Copy/move, update and deletion are
+unsupported. No sentinel key excludes extrema. Instances own all nodes with RAII;
+validate is an out-of-timing diagnostic traversal. See the frozen
+[structures_batch_v1 contract](STRUCTURES_PROTOCOL_v1.md) for precise invariants,
+exception semantics, timing and workload definitions.
+
+SkipList uses mt19937_64 seeded promotion with probability 1/2, maximum 32 levels,
+one new engine word per promotion attempt and its low bit as the decision.
+Duplicate insertion consumes no random words. Independent unique_ptr owners
+release nodes iteratively; forward chains are nonowning. Expected lookup/insertion
+is logarithmic while the cap suffices; worst work is linear and hard link storage
+is O(32U). Expectations assume independent promotion; no arbitrary-scale guarantee
+is inferred from the fixed cap.
+
+BTree uses even maximum child count M (minimum degree M/2), 4..64. Registry entries
+btree_m10, btree_m16, btree_m32 and btree_m64 select M directly. Top-down splitting
+promotes the median of a full M-1-key node; nonroot occupancy is M/2-1..M-1 keys.
+All leaves share a depth and internal nodes have keys+1 children. Nodes reserve
+entry/child capacity when created; ownership is unique_ptr and balanced recursive
+destruction has logarithmic depth. Linear node scans cost O(M log_M(U+1)); for
+fixed M this is O(log U), with O(U) owned storage. Duplicate lookup precedes
+mutation; there is no deletion implementation or alternative binary-tree variant.
+
+The structure registry is separate from array search because owned index lifetime,
+construction parameters and stored payloads do not fit vector function pointers.
+Normal lookup has no comparison counter. Memory complexities are theoretical;
+no isolated structure allocation or process RSS measurement is collected here.
